      "location": "Paragraph about the Rhine family (sentence about Pierce's dog)",
      "severity": "minor",
      "source_quote": "His name was Pierce, and he had a very fierce dog; at least he acted very fierce! He was kept behind a high wire fence connected to an old shed.",
      "suggested_fix": "Clarify the subtle nuance in the English: the dog was very fierce, or at least appeared fierce. The current Arabic «كان لديه كلب شرس جدًا؛ على الأقل كان يتصرّف بوحشيّة!» is understandable but slightly awkward. Suggested minor rewording to match the printed English nuance while remaining idiomatic: «كان اسمه بيرس، وكان لديه كلب شرس جدًّا — على الأقل بدا شديد الشراسة! كان محبوسًا خلف سياج سلكي عالٍ متصل بمستودعٍ قديم.»",
